      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The specification assumes equal index keys follow table scan order, but SQLite 3.51.0 gives the UNIQUE index of `t(k INTEGER PRIMARY KEY DESC, v UNIQUE) WITHOUT ROWID` an ascending `k` suffix, which reverses that order and can change failure rows selected by a limit. Fix: specify the actual index suffix order for constraint-created indexes and require duplicate detection to use it."
    }
